      "writtenOn": "2022-10-12T16:35:21Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Out of scope, but I see vaguely similar logic in `ide-config.sh` and various directions to set `-j` in docs. There isn\u0027t a great way to set the default parallelism in a makefile, and I\u0027m not sure we\u0027d want to. The closest thing would be setting `MAKEFLAGS` in the SDK environment, but that seems heavyhanded.\n\nTo the extent that we have shell scripts that invoke `make` and documentation that refers to it, it would be nice to set or suggest how to set `-j` in one place or in one way.",
      "revId": "b11fb2dec5a72d9117f40a377e2ef721cd3fe33b",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "f5cc5a4e_13750edc",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 1334530
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-10-17T23:59:00Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Right, I was hoping that load-average/max-load would help and that we could just change all the defaults to that, but it sounds like that might not be the best on all systems?\n\nRight, ideally this wouldn\u0027t have a dependency on the chroot.\nAny other suggestions?",
      "parentUuid": "beab4332_690e17fc",
      "revId": "b11fb2dec5a72d9117f40a377e2ef721cd3fe33b",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "f8d4c095_5d37ef50",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 1305927
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-10-18T16:33:58Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Most of our scripts set the desired parallelism to the number of cores. That basically means, \"This is what my computer is doing right now.\" I would say that\u0027s probably a good default for Chrome OS developers. I can\u0027t speak to what other people might want. Users can typically specify the arguments directly, so I\u0027m not too worried about just specifying the value in the chroot for that reason. What would bug me is if this happened because of some invisible setting that users of the chroot would probably not discover/know how to override by themselves.\n\nIt doesn\u0027t seem like there\u0027s an obvious way to do this generally. It might be a good idea to make a little snippet shell script for setting `-j` that you could source from other scripts. But that doesn\u0027t need to happen in this CL.",
      "parentUuid": "f5cc5a4e_13750edc",
      "revId": "b11fb2dec5a72d9117f40a377e2ef721cd3fe33b",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "dbd54038_606c450d",
        "filename": "util/compare_build.sh",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 196,
      "author": {
        "id": 1305927
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-10-12T16:35:21Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "It looks like this is already the default for `FLAGS_jobs`. Does this branch ever get taken?\n\nNit: Consider `-j --load-average\u003d$(nproc)`. You might want to experiment with the load target.",
      "revId": "b11fb2dec5a72d9117f40a377e2ef721cd3fe33b",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
